ted  faster i would love for there to be an  investigation maybe a committee report a  study something to find out what  happened i don't think that's ever going  to happen but it would just be great to  know like who's responsible and for them  to take accountability there's no other  other chance this is the only chance to  save my family  the malls in the meantime are just  hoping more months won't pass with them  sitting in ukraine  crystal gamansen global news  keefe  still ahead a raging fire shuts down a  major highway in california and forces  hundreds to flee  [Music]  a raging wildfires threatening homes  northwest of los angeles the alisal  wildfire has scorched almost 6 200  hectares in california's santa barbara  county and is just 5 percent contained  hundreds of people have fled their homes  and exxon mobil facility is being  closely monitored and a major highway  has been closed the fire is being fanned  by fierce sundowner winds that are  common in the area and have stoked some  of california's worst fires  early on wednesday hurricane pamela hit  mexico's pacific coast the resort city  of mazatlan was drenched with heavy rain  causing flash flooding at the height of  the storm wind gusts hit about 120  kilometers an hour pamela is expected to  be less intense as it moves inland  moving northeast into the u.s it's  likely to reach the texas border by  thursday  heading to the real final frontier next  william shatner makes space history  this newly released video shows what's  believed to be the world's first  delivery of donor lungs by an unmanned  drone the predawn flight took off from  toronto western hospital and six minutes  later touched down at toronto general  hospital it was a collaboration between  the city's university health network and  a quebec bioengineering company  logistics and time are huge factors in  organ transplants and drones could be  the future  well playing the captain of a starship  and actually going to the edge of space